---
import { STARTERS, starterSource, starterArchive } from './starters.mjs';
const { family, pilot = false } = Astro.props;
const directory = family === 'directory' || family === 'cards';
const base = '/raveldex/';
---
<p>Choose a project for your site. Each download includes the sample content, working pages and styles. Use Node 24 and npm; serve the built files over HTTP or HTTPS.</p>
{pilot && <p data-install-prerequisites>Index only public records. {directory ? <>Both directory presentations explicitly register native filters/facets for scalar <code>format</code> and multi-value <code>topics</code>. These title/link results need no snippet or section providers, native dialog, Popover or Intl.Segmenter. {family === 'directory' && <>The Astro project also selects original title/body source for static artifact reconstruction and needs Web Crypto on HTTPS or localhost. </>}{family === 'cards' && <>Rich display metadata is mapped by your application; images start off and require explicit visitor opt-in. </>}URL synchronization is selected in <code>configuration.mjs</code>: committed edits and pages push history; Back/Forward restores query, filters and page without new entries.</> : family === 'dropdown' ? <>The compact popup requires native Popover; the header form opens the complete results page when Popover is unavailable. This title/link starter needs no snippet, facet, section, worker or storage registration.</> : family === 'modal' ? <>Both modal projects require native <code>dialog</code>, <code>Intl.Segmenter</code> and Web Crypto on HTTPS or localhost. Anchored previews need selected source/section providers and exact original section text with anchors matching real headings; the Topic filter needs its facet registration.</> : <>Snippets require <code>Intl.Segmenter</code>; Astro also needs Web Crypto on HTTPS or localhost.</>} {family !== 'dropdown' && family !== 'cards' && <>Astro needs matching core/adapter package versions. </>}Registry installation below requires the exact versions to be available. For unpublished/local work, use the selected project's tarball instructions below. Rebuild and deploy pages and assets together after changing content, configuration or deployment base.</p>}
<div data-example-choice={pilot ? '' : undefined}>
{pilot && <div hidden data-choice-label><label for={`install-${family}`}>Installation platform</label><select id={`install-${family}`} data-choice-select>{STARTERS.filter(starter => starter.family === family).map(starter => <option value={starter.id}>{starter.id.endsWith('-astro') ? 'Astro' : 'Browser'}</option>)}</select></div>}
{STARTERS.filter(starter => starter.family === family).map(starter => {
  const astro = starter.id.endsWith('-astro');
  const stylesheet = astro ? 'src/style.css' : 'theme.css';
  const install = 'npm install @vmitsaras/raveldex@1.0.0' + (astro ? ' @vmitsaras/raveldex-astro@1.0.0' : '');
  return <section class="starter-setup__project" data-choice-panel={pilot ? starter.id : undefined} data-starter-id={starter.id} aria-labelledby={'starter-' + starter.id}>
    <h3 id={'starter-' + starter.id}>{starter.title}</h3>
    <div class="starter-setup__actions"><a href={base + `examples/${starter.id}/`}>Setup and replacement-data guide</a><a href={base + starterArchive(starter.id)} download>Download the complete starter</a></div>
    {pilot && <p data-package-guidance>For local/unpublished packages, substitute {astro ? 'matching core and Astro tarballs' : 'the core tarball'} in the install command: <code>{astro ? 'npm install /absolute/path/core.tgz /absolute/path/astro.tgz' : 'npm install /absolute/path/core.tgz'}</code>. Use the chosen project's pinned tooling and retain its generated lockfile.</p>}
    <ol data-starter-steps>
      <li>In an empty directory, extract <code>{`tar -xzf ${starter.id}.tar.gz --strip-components=1`}</code>. Read the setup guide for deployment paths and preview commands.</li>
      <li>Install from that directory with <code>{install}</code>, then run <code>npm run build</code> and <code>npm run preview</code> to try the sample content.</li>
      <li>{pilot && directory ? <>{astro ? <>Replace <code>entries</code> in <code>content.json</code>.</> : <>Replace the array in <code>content.json</code>.</>} Keep each <code>id</code> and <code>path</code> stable; update public <code>title</code>, <code>body</code>, scalar <code>format</code> and multi-value <code>topics</code>. Keep allowed group values and labels in <code>configuration.mjs</code> aligned with these records. {astro && <>Change <code>buildId</code> when content or configuration changes; the page's expected buildId must match the deployed manifest. </>}{family === 'cards' && <>In <code>load.mjs</code>, map only needed display fields: <code>excerpt</code>, <code>category</code>, <code>breadcrumb</code>, authored <code>date</code>, named <code>fields</code> and optional <code>image</code> URL/alternative/dimensions. These are display data, separate from native title/body indexing and format/topics filters. </>}Rebuild and deploy the complete pages and assets together.</> : pilot && family === 'modal' ? <>{astro ? <>Replace <code>entries</code> in <code>content.json</code>, keeping each <code>slug</code> stable.</> : <>Replace the array in <code>content.json</code>, keeping each <code>id</code> and <code>path</code> stable.</>} Update <code>title</code>, <code>category</code> and <code>sections</code>: retain each section's raw <code>anchor</code>, <code>heading</code> and {astro ? <code>text</code> : <code>body</code>}. The same records render the destination headings and derive original section ranges. {astro && <>Change <code>buildId</code> when content or configuration changes; the page's expected buildId must match the deployed manifest. </>}Rebuild and deploy the complete page/asset set together.</> : pilot && astro ? <>Replace <code>entries</code> in <code>content.json</code>: keep each <code>slug</code> stable and update <code>title</code>, <code>category</code> and <code>body</code>. Change <code>buildId</code> when content or configuration changes; the page's expected buildId must match the deployed manifest. Rebuild and deploy the complete page/asset set together.</> : <>Replace the public records in <code>content.json</code>, keeping IDs and destination paths stable.{astro && <> Change <code>buildId</code> when the content changes.</>} The guide explains the fields and any matching heading anchors. Rebuild after editing.</>}</li>
      <li>Change <code>{stylesheet}</code> using the theme recipe below. Rebuild, restart the preview and check search, links and keyboard focus with your own content.</li>
    </ol>
    <details><summary>View exact source files</summary><ul>{starter.files.map(path => <li><a href={base + starterSource(starter.id, path)}>{path}</a></li>)}</ul></details>
  </section>;
})}
</div>
